  <main id="main-content">
    <div id="poster">
      <div class="wrap">
        <section class="hero animate" aria-labelledby="poster-title">
          <header>
            <div>
              <div class="eyebrow">IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report · 2023</div>
              <h1 id="poster-title">Climate Change 2023: Key Findings</h1>
              <p class="lede"><span class="core">Human-caused climate change is unequivocal</span>, already affecting every region on Earth, and the window for meaningful action is rapidly closing.</p>
            </div>
            <aside class="report-box" aria-label="Poster context">
              <div class="label">Conference Poster</div>
              <div class="title">Evidence · Pathways · Urgency</div>
              <div class="meta">Academic, data-forward visual synthesis for researchers and policymakers.</div>
            </aside>
          </header>
        </section>

        <section class="metrics animate delay-1" aria-labelledby="metrics-title">
          <h2 id="metrics-title" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px;">Seven headline metrics</h2>
          <article class="metric card hot"><div class="num">1.1<small>°C</small></div><div class="label">Global surface temperature increase</div><div class="context">2011–2020 vs 1850–1900</div></article>
          <article class="metric card"><div class="num">410<small> ppm</small></div><div class="label">Atmospheric CO₂ concentration</div><div class="context">Highest in ≥2 million years</div></article>
          <article class="metric card"><div class="num">59<small> GtCO₂e</small></div><div class="label">Global GHG emissions</div><div class="context">2019 annual total</div></article>
          <article class="metric card"><div class="num">500<small> GtCO₂</small></div><div class="label">Remaining carbon budget for 1.5°C</div><div class="context">50% likelihood, from 2020</div></article>
          <article class="metric card urgent"><div class="num">43<small>%</small></div><div class="label">Required global GHG reduction by 2030 for a 1.5°C pathway</div><div class="context">Below 2019 levels · no/limited overshoot</div></article>
          <article class="metric card"><div class="num">0.20<small> m</small></div><div class="label">Observed sea level rise</div><div class="context">1901–2018</div></article>
          <article class="metric card population"><div class="num">3.3–3.6<small> bn</small></div><div class="label">People exposed to severe climate hazards</div><div class="context">Highly vulnerable contexts</div></article>
        </section>

        <div class="content-grid">
          <section class="card observed reveal" aria-labelledby="observed-title">
            <div class="section-title"><div class="kicker">01</div><h2 id="observed-title">Observed Changes and Current State</h2></div>
            <p class="section-copy">Warming, greenhouse gas concentrations, sea level rise, and cryosphere change are documented across multiple indicators. Extreme weather has increased in frequency and intensity in every region, with clear attribution to human influence.</p>
            <div class="observed-grid">
              <div class="obs-item"><div class="value">+1.1°C</div><div class="name">Warming above pre-industrial baseline</div></div>
              <div class="obs-item"><div class="value">~40%</div><div class="name">September Arctic sea-ice area loss, 1979–2020</div></div>
              <div class="obs-item"><div class="value">410 ppm</div><div class="name">CO₂ concentration reached in 2019</div></div>
              <div class="obs-item"><div class="value">~0.20 m</div><div class="name">Global mean sea-level rise, 1901–2018</div></div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="card chart-panel reveal" aria-labelledby="projection-title">
            <div class="section-title"><div class="kicker">02</div><h2 id="projection-title">Future Projections Under SSP Scenarios</h2></div>
            <p class="section-copy">Pathway choices define late-century warming: very low emissions hold best-estimate warming near <strong>1.4°C</strong>, while very high emissions reach <strong>4.4°C</strong> by 2100.</p>
            <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="scenarioChart" role="img" aria-label="Projected global warming by 2100 across SSP scenarios from 1.4 to 4.4 degrees Celsius"></canvas></div>
            <div class="scenario-note" aria-hidden="true">
